  "limits": [
    "the readouts are empirical laws estimated from an auxiliary stream, not the engine's readout; they bracket prediction quality rather than measure a learner",
    "one declared entity transition is withheld; whether that is the right size or pair is a pre-run enumeration question and is not settled here",
    "three design-block seeds per configuration measure the estimator; they do not authorise the run and they are not the confirmatory block",
    "the wrong-law control is a uniform law, and a constant predictor's per-position loss has zero variance, so its per-world standard error is exactly 0.0 and the control brackets nothing: it shows the ceiling is not the worst possible readout, not how wrong a wrong law would score",
    "this world is a reconstruction of the scale family (six entities in two groups, the same arrival fraction, noise rate and twelve events a cycle) and not `phase_l_campaign.build_world`, and no `DI` onset has been measured on it: the predictor side of the protocol is untested in the world that now carries the outcome",
    "the confirmation cycles are the protocol's medians, so the window position is plausible rather than observed"
  ]
